From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krane <chris@krane.dev>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:49:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hyprconfigurator): skip the write when nothing changed

Port of pctrade/end4-pC dc2ca2600ee6: none (krane-only)
https://github.com/pctrade/end4-pC/tree/dc2ca2600ee6d7852bf0ac91361db8e510f90a74
Problem: re-applying border colors on every configreloaded would rewrite shellOverrides/main.lua, which triggers another reload.
Port: krane-only
Drop when: the pinned hyprconfigurator.py compares before writing.
---
 .../quickshell/ii/scripts/hyprland/hyprconfigurator.py      | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/scripts/hyprland/hyprconfigurator.py b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/scripts/hyprland/hyprconfigurator.py
index 10bf4ea7..bf4528a6 100755
--- a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/scripts/hyprland/hyprconfigurator.py
+++ b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/scripts/hyprland/hyprconfigurator.py
@@ -85,6 +85,12 @@ def edit_hyprland_config(file_path, set_args, reset_args):
                     new_lines[-1] += '\n'
                 new_lines.append(generate_config_line(key, value))
                 
+    # Unchanged content: skip the write. Hyprland reloads on every write to this
+    # file, and the shell re-applies border colors on every reload, so writing
+    # the same content again would loop.
+    if os.path.exists(file_path) and "".join(new_lines) == "".join(lines):
+        return
+
     dir_name = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(file_path))
     os.makedirs(dir_name, exist_ok=True)
     temp_path = None
